TITLE:Rec Dec Traditions
H1:Rec dec traditions: twelve new ones for the Recreation Deck <span class="draft">pitch for the user's approval · plan only</span>
SUB:The user (2026-10-19): when the rec dec is switched on (after Pillar 5's Steps 3 and 4), it comes with about a dozen traditions of its own, "Sunday Lightdisc tournament, that kind of thing". Here are twelve: sport, quiet, social, creative and seasonal, fitted round the ship's existing traditions and the approved events plan. Each uses what the rec dec already has (the Lightdisc game, the tap-to-play pool, kayaks, wall and float room, the auditorium stage). Written by the Pillar 5 designer for lead 16. No game code.
NAV:plain=In plain words|week=The week|list=The twelve|fit=How they fit|q=Questions

<section id="plain">
  <h2>In plain words</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Twelve new traditions</b>, all on the rec dec, on top of the five the rec dec plan already has (Winner Stays On on Sundays, the river regatta and Ring the bell every four weeks, Saturday film night and talent night in the auditorium).</li>
    <li><b>A mix:</b> four sporty (the Lightdisc Cup, Rookie court, Lanes night, Paddle club), three active-but-easy (Dawn swim, Wall night, Zero-G games), two quiet (Float hour, Glow paddle), two creative or social (Open stage, Wren talks) and one seasonal party (Season splash; Glow paddle is seasonal too).</li>
    <li><b>Nothing new to learn:</b> you join the way you join any tradition (be there, or tap a person or a place to join in); the sporty ones use the Lightdisc game and the pool, kayak, wall and float room animations the rec dec already plans. No times or scores except where Lightdisc already keeps them.</li>
    <li><b>Small rewards:</b> a little leisure and social, sometimes energy or hygiene, a friendship step with whoever hosts or plays beside you, a name on the foyer's boards. Never a penalty for not going.</li>
    <li><b>No staff:</b> the rec dec has none (the user's answer), so each tradition is hosted by a crew member who loves it.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="week">
  <h2>The week, with the new ones beside the old</h2>
  <p class="note"><span class="tag new">gold</span> new rec dec tradition · <span class="tag">teal</span> rec dec tradition already planned · plain text: the ship's existing traditions elsewhere (for the clashes). Day 1 is a Monday. "4-wk" and "2-wk" run every four or two weeks.</p>
  <div class="week">
    <div class="day"><h4>Monday</h4><p>Gym club · Lap of the Wren · Sunrise stretch · Book circle (2-wk) · Department cup (4-wk) · the Captain's all-hands (first Monday of a season)</p><p><span class="tag new">Rookie court 19:00</span> <span class="tag new">Wren talks 20:00 (4-wk)</span></p></div>
    <div class="day"><h4>Tuesday</h4><p>Knit and natter · Spice shelf supper · Tiles night · Open lab (4-wk) · Bridge hour (4-wk)</p><p><span class="tag new">Dawn swim 06:15</span> <span class="tag new">Wall night 18:30</span></p></div>
    <div class="day"><h4>Wednesday</h4><p>Pick-your-own breakfast · Sunrise stretch · Brennan's tasting table · Open door · Late piano</p><p><span class="tag new">Paddle club 18:30</span> <span class="tag new">Open stage 19:00</span> <span class="tag new">Float hour 21:30</span></p></div>
    <div class="day"><h4>Thursday</h4><p>Postcard night · Late piano · Quiz night 20:00</p><p><span class="tag new">Dawn swim 06:15</span></p></div>
    <div class="day"><h4>Friday</h4><p>Sunrise stretch · Works Friday tea · Music jam · Tap night</p><p><span class="tag new">Lanes night 19:00 (2-wk)</span></p></div>
    <div class="day"><h4>Saturday</h4><p>Long breakfast · Garden hour · Cook-along · Tiles ladder · Harvest morning (2-wk) · Sowing morning (season) · Observatory night</p><p><span class="tag">Film night 20:00</span> <span class="tag new">Zero-G games 15:00 (4-wk)</span> <span class="tag new">Season splash 14:00 (season)</span> <span class="tag new">Glow paddle 21:30 (season)</span></p></div>
    <div class="day"><h4>Sunday</h4><p>Sunday swap meet · Sunday long table · Reading corner</p><p><span class="tag">Regatta / Ring the bell 09:30 (4-wk)</span> <span class="tag">Winner Stays On 11:30</span> <span class="tag new">Lightdisc Cup 11:30 (4-wk, in place of Winner Stays On)</span> <span class="tag">Talent night 19:30 (4-wk)</span></p></div>
  </div>
  <p class="note">No two rec dec traditions share a room at the same time (the events check's rule). The evening ones end before quiz night (20:00 Thursday) and leave the Commons their crowd: each draws 6-12 people, inside the rec dec's evening cap of about 15; the Cup and Lanes night are gatherings (exempt from the cap, like talent night).</p>
</section>

<section id="list">
  <h2>The twelve</h2>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <tr><th>Tradition</th><th>When · where</th><th>Who</th><th>What you do</th><th>You get</th><th>First</th></tr>
    <tr><td><b>The Lightdisc Cup</b><br><span class="note">sport · the user's example</span></td><td>Every four weeks, Sunday 11:30-16:30 (the Sunday between a regatta and Ring the bell) · Lightdisc court and stands</td><td>Pell runs the bracket on the foyer chalkboard; teams of two from each department; the stands full (a gathering)</td><td>Enter with a partner (tap Pell, pick a friend) and play your matches in the Lightdisc game, or cheer from the stands. Eight pairs, three rounds, a final at 16:00.</td><td>leisure and social; a friendship step with your partner; reputation with your department if you go far; the winners' names on the foyer's Cup board and a small cup on the shelf for four weeks</td><td>Day 28 (then 56, 84 ...). That Sunday it takes Winner Stays On's slot.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>Rookie court</b><br><span class="note">sport · gentle</span></td><td>Mondays 19:00-20:00 · Lightdisc court</td><td>Pell coaches anyone new; juniors and the curious</td><td>Tap Pell to join a slow practice game (the Lightdisc game with a gentler ball); Pell's tips between points.</td><td>leisure; a friendship step with Pell over the weeks; your first Lightdisc win (a line in your Record)</td><td>Day 8 (the evening the Space Creature swims off)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>Dawn swim</b><br><span class="note">active · quiet</span></td><td>Tuesdays and Thursdays 06:15-06:45 · the pool</td><td>Rina, before the infirmary opens; three or four early risers</td><td>Tap a lane: the swimming animation, the hull windows, the stars.</td><td>hygiene and energy topped up for the morning; a friendship step with Rina over a few weeks</td><td>Day 2</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>Wall night</b><br><span class="note">active</span></td><td>Tuesdays 18:30-19:45 · the climbing wall in the river hall</td><td>Tomas belays (the stars and somewhere new: he loves heights); four to eight climbers</td><td>Tap the wall to climb a route (the climbing animation); ring the bell at the top if you like.</td><td>leisure; a friendship step with Tomas; your name on the season's bell board (shared with Ring the bell)</td><td>Day 2 (and Day 9, the evening after your test job)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>Paddle club</b><br><span class="note">sport · social</span></td><td>Wednesdays 18:30-19:30 · the river hall</td><td>Chief Holt teaches the slow loop (he watches the water like a hawk); a handful of paddlers</td><td>Tap the kayak dock to paddle the slow loop, then the fast run once Holt says you're ready (after three visits).</td><td>leisure; Holt warms to you (a rare thing); the regatta's "fun heat" feels earned</td><td>Day 3</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>Open stage</b><br><span class="note">creative</span></td><td>Wednesdays 19:00-20:30 · the auditorium stage</td><td>Comms Chief Lucia Ferreira opens the stage; musicians and anyone rehearsing for talent night; Maeve Volkov on the lights</td><td>Sit and listen, or tap the stage to try a piece (the talent night act picker: a tune, a poem, a joke); good practice before you sign up.</td><td>leisure and social; Lucia remembers you at talent night; the Halden tune (Echo Signal) is played here from Day 25 on</td><td>Day 3</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>Float hour</b><br><span class="note">quiet</span></td><td>Wednesdays 21:30-22:15 · the float room</td><td>Matthias Oduya (who keeps the quiet watch) dims the orbs; quiet music; no talking</td><td>Tap to float: the slow-motion drift animation; you can stay the whole hour.</td><td>rest and mood (a calmer night's sleep after); a nod from Matthias</td><td>Day 3</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>Lanes night</b><br><span class="note">sport · departments</span></td><td>Every two weeks, Friday 19:00-20:00 · the pool and its gallery</td><td>Department relay teams of four (one per lane); Holt starts it, the gallery cheers (a gathering)</td><td>Swim a leg for Works (tap the lane when it's your turn) or cheer from the gallery. The finishing order is seeded from the day, never from your speed.</td><td>social; reputation with Works when you swim; the winning department's pennant over the pool for two weeks</td><td>Day 12 (then 26: the evening of Calder's question)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>Zero-G games</b><br><span class="note">silly · active</span></td><td>Every four weeks, Saturday 15:00-16:30 · the float room</td><td>Pell and Rina run it: orb catch, slow-motion tag, the "drift relay"</td><td>Tap someone to join their team; a few rounds of the float animation with a little score of orbs caught (seeded).</td><td>leisure and lots of social; laughter lines in chatter for a day</td><td>Day 6 (your free first weekend)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>Wren talks</b><br><span class="note">social · learning</span></td><td>Every four weeks, Monday 20:00-20:45 · the auditorium</td><td>One crew member gives a short talk: Dr. Sato on what lives between the stars, Torres on the drive coils, Brennan on spice, Calder on the Wren's first refit; Vance chairs</td><td>Sit and listen (a short meeting panel, one question you can ask). Later, as an Engine Specialist, you can be asked to give one.</td><td>a little social and a "learned" note in the Ship app; a friendship step with the speaker if you ask a question</td><td>Day 8 (Sato's first talk: the creature that just swam off)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>Season splash</b><br><span class="note">seasonal party</span></td><td>The second Saturday of each season, 14:00-16:30 · the pool and the river hall</td><td>The whole deck: inflatables in the pool, the wave gate on, Brennan's ice lollies, music; Pell and Rina organise</td><td>Tap anything: the pool, the kayaks, the slide into the shallow end (the animations); hang about with friends.</td><td>leisure and social for the afternoon; the season's banner over the foyer</td><td>Day 13 (with the Veyli guests aboard: they love warm water)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>Glow paddle</b><br><span class="note">quiet · seasonal</span></td><td>The last Saturday of each season, 21:30-22:30 · the river hall, lights off</td><td>Holt leads it; kayaks with little lanterns drift the slow loop in the dark, stars through the port windows</td><td>Tap the dock to paddle with a lantern, or watch from the pebble beach.</td><td>mood and social; a quiet friendship step with whoever you paddle beside</td><td>Day 90 (the end of Sowing; then 181, 272, 363)</td></tr>
  </table></div>
</section>

<section id="fit">
  <h2>How they fit (traditions, events, career)</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>What they move or replace:</b> the Lightdisc Cup takes Winner Stays On's Sunday slot once every four weeks (Winner Stays On runs the other three). Nothing else moves; the junior common room stays the quiet Saturday hangout.</li>
    <li><b>The events plan (approved v4):</b> traditions pause in an event's hardest phases, as now. The storm (Days 4-5) pauses Thursday's Dawn swim only after 14:00, so nothing is lost. Day 8's Space Creature leaves at 18:40, before Rookie court and Sato's talk (which is about it). Day 13's Season splash happens with the Veyli aboard. Day 17's power surge is over by 15:00; Day 18's Echo Signal (20:30) is a Thursday, when the rec dec only has the dawn swim. Day 21's distress call (11:30-16:30) pauses Winner Stays On that afternoon (the regatta at 09:30 finishes first). Day 24's Loss of Power is a morning.</li>
    <li><b>The career's big days:</b> nothing on the rec dec is aimed at you on Days 9-11, 15-16, 22-23 or 26; Dawn swim before the Day 9 test and Wall night after it are there if you want them. On the night shift (Days 19-20) you sleep through Friday's Lanes night; it's a week off anyway.</li>
    <li><b>Holidays</b> (on hold): none clash if they return.</li>
    <li><b>Buildable with what exists:</b> the tradition engine (weekly, two-weekly, four-weekly and seasonal rhythms are all there), tap-to-join, the gatherings, the rec dec's planned animations and Lightdisc game, the talent night act picker and the meeting panel. New: the Cup's bracket (a small seeded draw), the boards' names, and a gentler Lightdisc ball for Rookie court.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="q">
  <h2>Questions for the user (with my recommendations)</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><b>Twelve, or fewer to start?</b> <i>Recommended: all twelve; the rec dec has a lot of rooms, and most are small.</i></li>
    <li><b>The Lightdisc Cup in place of Winner Stays On one Sunday in four?</b> <i>Recommended: yes, so Sunday afternoon is always Lightdisc and once a month it's the big one.</i></li>
    <li><b>Do you play the Cup's matches yourself</b> (the live Lightdisc game), or are they settled for you? <i>Recommended: you play them; the other pairs' results are seeded.</i></li>
    <li><b>Lanes night results seeded</b> (never your speed)? <i>Recommended: yes, like the regatta: it's about turning up for your department.</i></li>
    <li><b>Glow paddle once a season</b> (four a year), or once a year? <i>Recommended: once a season, so a long game sees it.</i></li>
    <li><b>Wren talks: can you give one later</b> (as an Engine Specialist, on the drive)? <i>Recommended: yes, a small moment after the career arc (a talk on the drive coils, with Torres in the front row).</i></li>
  </ol>
</section>
